            <ArticleTitle>Laser-Initiated Radical Trifluoromethylation of Peptides and Proteins: Application to Mass-Spectrometry-Based Protein Footprinting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>14007-14010</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/anie.201706697</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Described is a novel, laser-initiated radical trifluoromethylation for protein footprinting and its broad residue coverage. . CF3 reacts with 18 of the 20 common amino acids, including Gly, Ala, Ser, Thr, Asp, and Glu, which are relatively silent with regard to . OH. This new approach to footprinting is a bridge between trifluoromethylation in materials and medicinal chemistry and structural biology and biotechnology. Its application to a membrane protein and to myoglobin show that the approach is sensitive to protein conformational change and solvent accessibility.</AbstractText>
